        "quote": "There are three classifications of mixed use districts as follows:",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.185.020:block:0#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.185.020 block 1",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 1,
          "component_id": "2fd0ad9e-eaa4-539d-853d-d8bb728b63b3",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 568,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.185.020:block:1",
          "start": 67
        },
        "quote": "(a) X-1 Mixed Use District. This district facilitates a compatible mixed use activity center within a traditional residential neighborhood and, to a limited extent, in areas envisioned for mixed use development by the comprehensive plan. The district includes a balance of compatible residential, office, civic, and neighborhood commercial retail/service uses of low to moderate intensity that complement and support dense neighborhood residential areas and pedestrian usage with quality urban design.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.185.020:block:1#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.185.020 block 2",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 2,
          "component_id": "d5ef4bd3-6a91-53d7-9553-0c52b8192f57",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 861,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.185.020:block:2",
          "start": 569
        },
        "quote": "(b) X-2 Mixed Use District. This district facilitates a mixed use area that transitions from a higher intensity industrial use area to lower intensity neighborhood-scale residential areas and includes a balance of compatible residential, office, commercial service, and light industrial uses.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.185.020:block:2#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.185.020 block 3",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 3,
          "component_id": "5093063b-e5f9-510b-8d65-f33925909ba7",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1130,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.185.020:block:3",
          "start": 862
        },
        "quote": "(c) X-3 Mixed Use District. This district facilitates a destination-oriented mixed use district in the area known as the North Crossings area of North Topeka that serves as the northern entertainment/cultural anchor of downtown. The objectives of the district include:",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.185.020:block:3#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.185.020 block 4",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 4,
          "component_id": "b4e83b27-058b-5fb4-8a61-8f9f3c57cdc2",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1258,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.185.020:block:4",
          "start": 1131
        },
        "quote": "(1) Improving the area as a 24-hour destination for urban, cultural, entertainment, community, and residential experiences; and",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.185.020:block:4#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.185.020 block 5",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 5,
          "component_id": "c8e7c449-8bce-5567-be3b-1e97f38b0521",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1413,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.185.020:block:5",
          "start": 1259
        },
        "quote": "(2) Retention and attraction of businesses, workplaces and residences through adaptive reuse and rehabilitation of existing buildings as a preference; and",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.185.020:block:5#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
